# Starter pack development workspace

This project **is** the Agent Starter Pack (rules, skills, MCP, install scripts).

**Hard stop:** **`pack-only-edit-boundary.mdc`** — edit **only** the open workspace root (this pack checkout, wherever it lives on disk). Other repos named in docs are read-only references; never modify them from this workspace.

**Recommendations:** **`agent-recommendation-discipline.mdc`** — default first; scope before execute; optional extras need mechanism + blast radius + “skip unless.”

## Rule layers

| Folder | Applies to |
|--------|------------|
| **`.cursor/rules/`** (repo root) | **The load path.** Four workspace-only rules (edit boundary, recommendation discipline, audit, starter-pack-repo) **plus every generic rule synced from `pack/rules/`** |
| **`pack/rules/`** | **Canonical source, not a load path** — generic only; never workspace-specific boundaries |

**Never edit a synced copy in `.cursor/rules/`.** Edit `pack/rules/`, then re-run
`pack\scripts\sync-project-rules.ps1 -ProjectRoot (Get-Location).Path`. The same script with
`-VerifyOnly` reports drift, and it compares the files themselves — which is why no count is written
here. A hardcoded total went stale twice, at 13 and again when the fourteenth rule landed.

**Why they are here (WQ-456).** `install.ps1` also copies them to `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\rules\`, and
**Cursor does not load that folder.** It is not one of the four rule locations Cursor documents, and
this workspace proved it: `full-paths-in-chat.mdc` was `alwaysApply: true`, present in the profile, and
absent from agent context for months. A project's `.cursor/rules/` **is** loaded, so that is where an
always-on rule has to live.

Before new agent docs anywhere: **`pack/rules/generic-agent-doc-hygiene.mdc`**.

**Read first:** `pack/docs/START_HERE.md` — install paths, agent pre-flight, bootstrap, audit maintenance, pitfalls.

**No per-machine files in this checkout.** The folder is meant to be copied, cloned and downloaded, so
the agent-context artifacts (`AGENT_CONTEXT.json`, `AGENT_REFRESH.md`, `AGENT_PASTE.txt`,
`AGENT_SESSION_START.md`) are written to a machine-local state directory **outside** it —
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\AgentStarterPack\state\<checkout>`. There is no `docs/AGENT_SESSION_START.md` here and
that is correct; run `Refresh-AgentContext.cmd` and read the paths it prints. Do not "fix" their
absence by writing them into `docs/`.

- Do not mix other application code here.
- Do not run sync/bootstrap scripts that write into other projects unless the user explicitly opens that project for editing.
- User-global install copies to `%USERPROFILE%\.cursor\AgentStarterPack\`.
- Verify: `pack\scripts\doctor.ps1 -ProjectRoot (Get-Location).Path` and `run_audit.cmd` (pack self-audit)
- Export for other PCs: `export.ps1`
- After audit-system edits: `pack\scripts\sync-audit-system.ps1` then verify exit 0

Documentation index: `pack/docs/README.md`
